<!--Engine Documentation — RenderOutput
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender.documentation.RenderOutput-->
<edoc:RenderOutput xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:edoc="org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    What engine methods return
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Every engine method returns RenderOutput. The compiler treats that value as
    opaque. BlockML requires no file and no 1:1 input-to-output mapping. A call
    may produce zero files, one file, many files, or side effects only.

    File-based targets conventionally use:

        interface FilesRenderOutput {
          files: { path: string; content: string; sourceMap?: string }[]
          sideEffects?: RenderSideEffect[]
        }

    files may be empty when the only result is a side effect. The side-effect
    shape is target-defined. This package does not invent a MachineBlocks file
    layout; the SCAD target specifies .scad paths and optional .scad.map entries.

    copyTemplate's output is the copied file recorded in files (or an equivalent
    side effect the host writes). renderTemplate's output is the substituted
    template text. compile's output is whatever the processor's compile callback
    produced — the engine wraps that result; it does not parse SCAD.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="edoc:Introduction" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</edoc:RenderOutput>
